{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver met limbs (a) and (b) of POL-NS-01 on clean telemetry. The trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 2026-09-18T15:03:52, and the driver's device trace — a full-coverage 205-fix record at 10 s cadence with no gaps — places him inside the 150 m AIRPORT arrival radius for 54 consecutive qualifying fixes, that run beginning at 15:03:50, two seconds before the arrived event. Under POL-NS-02 the AIRPORT radius is 150 m, and there are far more than the three consecutive in-radius fixes that clause requires, so arrival at the pin is proved, not merely asserted.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00618", "EV-TRIP-00618"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (c) is met with 50 seconds to spare. The driver held position inside the pickup geofence in one continuous run of 530 seconds, first fix 15:03:50 and last 15:12:40, against a minimum dwell of 480 seconds for the AIRPORT zone class; and the clock is measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, not from the arrived tap, exactly as POL-NS-01 directs. The derived shortfall is minus 50 seconds — that is, a surplus, not a deficit.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00618"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider cannot retreat behind POL-NS-05. That clause's distance trigger fires only where the arrived marker sits more than 300 m from the pin, and the trace's single in-geofence interval in which the driver held position begins at 15:03:50, before the 15:03:52 marker; at the marker the driver's admissible position was inside the 150 m arrival radius and therefore cannot be more than 300 m out. There is no false-arrival event here, and limb (iii) of POL-NS-05 confirms that even a sloppy marker would not defeat a dwell that meets the minimum.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00618", "EV-TRIP-00618"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.first_ts",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No shortfall exists for the rider to recover under POL-NS-06. The effective dwell of 530 seconds exceeds the 480 second AIRPORT minimum by 50 seconds, so the clause's full-refund route is closed on its own arithmetic without the driver needing to accumulate dwell across separate intervals. I disclose that the traffic advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-00618-01 is MISSING — issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0 — but this claim does not rest on it: no advisory-excused accumulation is required, so the absence affects nothing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00618", "EV-ADVIS-00618-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The clauses that would refund the fee and pay the driver nothing cannot run. POL-NS-04 limb (a) needs at least one locating or coordinating message from the rider in the chat log, and the chat log for this trip holds zero messages; limb (c) needs the rider's device within the 200 m AIRPORT presence radius for the majority of qualifying fixes, and it never is — 0 of the rider's 41 fixes qualify, his fixes sitting between roughly 249 m and 258 m from the pin throughout. With both limbs unavailable, the rider-exoneration route fails and nothing displaces the driver's entitlement.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00618", "EV-GPS-00618"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.rider_qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-NS-07 anti-farming guard does not trip, and the schedule amount is the sum the driver has put in dispute. driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the threshold of 4, and 1 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 110 is 0.009, below the 0.08 rate, so both limbs of the check fail to bite. On the SGD 6.00 AIRPORT zone-class fee the 80 percent compensation rate yields SGD 4.80 — precisely the contested amount.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00618", "EV-FARE-00618"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver does not stretch the record, and the tribunal should note what he does not claim. The trip record shows status COMPLETED, started_at 15:12:50, ended_at 15:34:40, cancelled_by null and cancellation_reason_code null. It therefore does not show the trip terminated by the driver with RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT, and limb (d) of POL-NS-01 is not made out on this record. The driver does not ask the tribunal to read a cancellation into a completed trip. That is the one gap in his case; arrival, radius, dwell, the absence of any displacing clause and a clean anti-farming profile are all proved on weight 1.0 evidence above.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00618"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing on either profile sends this case away from a decision on the merits, and both files are cited only for the tests the general policy names. rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0 and rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are both 0, so neither POL-NS-09(c) nor POL-NS-09(d) fires; no abuse pattern exists on either side to justify holding the case back from a ruling.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00618", "EV-DPROF-00618"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{"ruling":{"ruling":"NO_ACTION","amount_sgd":null,"driver_compensation_sgd":null,"referrals":[],"confidence":0.9,"explanation":"Driver — you did on the ground what you say you did, and I accept all of it. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00618, weight 1.0, 205 fixes at 10 s cadence, no gaps) places you inside the 150 m Changi T3 arrival radius from 15:03:50 to 15:12:40 — a single continuous in-geofence hold of 530 seconds against the 480-second AIRPORT minimum — and your 'arrived' tap at 15:03:52 follows the first qualifying fix, so POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (b) and POL-NS-02 are met, and limb (c) is met with 50 seconds to spare (derived shortfall minus 50 s, i.e. a surplus). POL-NS-05 does not catch you: no false-arrival marker exists, and POL-NS-06 has no shortfall to work on. But arrival is not the case you have to make; a no-show is. POL-NS-01 is conjunctive and limb (d) requires the trip to have been terminated by you with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT at or after the dwell elapsed. The trip record (EV-TRIP-00618, weight 1.0) shows the opposite: status COMPLETED, cancelled_at null, cancelled_by null, cancellation_reason_code null, with the meter running 15:12:50 to 15:34:40 over 16.5 km from Changi T3 to Paya Lebar Square. The passenger boarded and you drove him. No no-show occurred, so no cancellation fee arises, and POL-NS-07 pays you 80 percent of that fee only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full — it is not. The SGD 4.80 you seek (80 percent of the SGD 6.00 AIRPORT zone fee) is therefore not payable, and the fare breakdown's own money block (EV-FARE-00618, weight 1.0) computes your compensation at SGD 0.00. The anti-farming guard does not trip on your profile — driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1 against 110 completed trips, a rate of 0.009, both below the thresholds of 4 and 0.08 — but that is moot, because the entitlement never arises. Your own submission concedes the point, noting that the record does not show a termination on a no-show reason code and that this is 'the one gap' in the case; I agree, and it is decisive. Your assertion in the claim that 'the rules say I get compensated for waiting beyond the minimum' cites no clause in this policy, and no clause in this category creates a waiting payment on a trip that ran to completion.

Rider — there is no contested charge on your ledger for any ruling to move. The fare breakdown itemises cancellation_fee SGD 0.00 and waiting_time_fee SGD 0.00 against total_charged SGD 29.08 (base 3.80 + distance 12.38 + time 6.10 + airport surcharge 6.00 + platform fee 0.80), payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd SGD 0.00. The SGD 29.08 is simply the metered fare for the trip you actually took, and the '-6.00' difference published in the derived money block is the schedule fee of SGD 6.00 set against a fee_charged of SGD 0.00 — a record that no cancellation fee was ever billed. Nothing is owed to you and nothing is recoverable from you for a no-show. Your account of the pickup (that you walked your luggage to the car and were told coming to the door was 'not my job') is consistent with a completed trip and is noted, but no clause in this category produces a refund or a referral on it.

Both parties on the subordinate routes: POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider here — the chat log holds zero messages and the rider's 41 fixes sit between about 249 m and 258 m from the pin, outside the 200 m AIRPORT presence radius, so limbs (a) and (c) both fail — but that route was never engaged, since no fee was charged to refund. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00618-01 is MISSING (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0, therefore it can carry no fact and its absence is all that is citable); neither side needs it, because no dwell accumulation under POL-NS-06(i) is required. No escalation trigger fires: confidence is above the 0.70 floor; the artifacts do not contradict each other on arrival, dwell or presence; rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0 and the counterparty dispute counters are both 0; the anti-farming check does not trip; and the deciding facts rest on weight 1.0 material. Referrals: none — no clause here (POL-NS-05(ii) false-arrival record, POL-NS-07 escalation packet) produces one. The present state stands: the driver's claim is not supported and the charge stands as it presently is. Confidence 0.9, capped at 1.0 by the weight-1.0 artifacts (trip record and fare breakdown) that carry the deciding fact."},"discarded_claims":[]}
